Notice for internal/css

Go files in this directory follow or name source files of Blink, the layout
engine of Chromium. The license of each Blink file was read from the header
of the file at the tag 156.0.8078.4 of
https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src, the version of the reference
browser.

  color.go   The parser and the printer of a color follow
             css_parser_fast_paths.cc (BSD-3-Clause), color.cc
             (BSD-2-Clause, with the copyright of Apple in the file) and
             ui/gfx/color_conversions.cc (BSD-3-Clause).
  cssom.go   The file reproduces how Chromium handles an inline style
             through the CSSOM. It names no upstream file that it ports.
             One comment names a function of css_property_value_set.cc
             (LGPL-2.0-or-later). The serializer of the CSSOM in Blink is
             style_property_serializer.cc and css_primitive_value.cc
             (LGPL-2.0-or-later). The Go file does not say if it follows
             those two files.

  calc.go    The value of a CSS math function follows
             css_math_expression_node.cc (BSD-3-Clause, with the copyright
             of Google in the file).
  content.go The parser of the property content and of a CSS string
             follows css_tokenizer.cc, css_parser_idioms.cc and
             longhands_custom.cc (BSD-3-Clause). SerializeString is the
             algorithm "serialize a string" of the CSS Object Model
             specification. Blink has that algorithm in css_markup.cc
             (LGPL-2.0-or-later), which the Go file names and does not
             follow. A probe recorded the strings that Chromium prints
             (../browser/testdata/pagesheets-cases.json.gz).

decl.go and range.go port no upstream file.

NOTICE-Blink.txt in this directory has the first comment of each Blink file
above that has its license terms in the file, with its copyright lines. The
text of the GNU Library General Public License, version 2, is in
../browser/LICENSE-LGPL-2.0.txt. The license of the Blink files that say
"Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license" is in
../font/LICENSE-Chromium.txt.

The owner of the repository has not decided what to do with the code that
follows the LGPL files. The options are in docs/LICENSE-AUDIT.md, finding
F1. This notice states where the code comes from. It does not put the Go
files under a license.
